WEBVTT

00:02:57.882 --> 00:03:01.377
and society and culture generally

00:03:01.401 --> 00:03:03.446
and what we might do about that.

00:03:03.470 --> 00:03:06.783
Methinks there's a connection.
I think you think there's a connection.

00:03:06.807 --> 00:03:09.678
DB: I think there's a connection, yeah.
CA: Deep connection.

00:03:09.702 --> 00:03:11.223
CA: So let's try and do that.

00:03:11.247 --> 00:03:15.436
I mean, David, start by just telling me
the basic thesis of the book.

00:03:15.460 --> 00:03:17.434
DB: Well, it occurred to me this morning,

00:03:17.458 --> 00:03:19.783
the book is about
the central lie of our culture,

00:03:19.807 --> 00:03:21.947
and that lie is, "I can
make myself happy,"

00:03:21.971 --> 00:03:25.746
that if I earn some success,
if I have more exciting experiences,

00:03:25.770 --> 00:03:27.321
that if I get a little thinner,

00:03:27.345 --> 00:03:29.143
I can be happy and fulfilled.

00:03:29.167 --> 00:03:30.692
And that's a useful lie to have.